<h2>Asobi 0.2 (build 241)</h2>
<p><b>Sign in to Kitsu as yourself.</b></p>
<ul>
<li>The Review List panel has an <b>Account</b> row: sign in with your Kitsu email and password and Asobi acts as you — <b>comments carry your name</b> in Kitsu, and the project list is exactly the productions <b>you're assigned to</b>. Kitsu's own permissions do the scoping.</li>
<li>Your password goes straight to your Kitsu server; only the resulting token is kept, in your keychain. Two-factor accounts get a code field when Kitsu asks. If your sign-in expires, the panel says so.</li>
<li>Signed out, Asobi uses the studio bot token as before — the right identity for a supervisor's own seat and the overnight watcher.</li>
</ul>
]]></description>
